{"agent":"bgb","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The name pass now treats every `load_reviewers` name and model as a redact token, including the `reviewer.configured` subject that `pending_reviewer_name` (ddflow/services/gates/reviewers.py) is changed to trust as verbatim. Given a configured reviewer `name = \"local-reviewer-f8f8\"`, appending `reviewer.configured` stores `[REDACTED:name]` in the shard; after replay `state.reviewer_writes[dig][\"name\"]` is that placeholder (or missing), and the new `return str(name or evidence[\"reviewer\"])` hands the gate a redacted identity, so the pending local reviewer no longer matches. The same pass also strips public reviewers: `name = \"gemini\"` / `model = \"gemini-2.5-flash\"` disappears from later shards, not only the git-ignored local layer.","digest":"9acfbedcfffa569e","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_reviewer_redact_names","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_reviewer_redact_names"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression only appends one fresh `gate.failed` against `.ddflow/reviewers.toml`. It never reloads state, never covers the `reviewers.py` return path, and does not rewrite the five shards that already contain the name, so those committed copies still publish it and a replay of `reviewer.configured` is untested.","digest":"c3cf272ed5d9b2cf","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_log_redaction_reviewer_names.py:test_a_local_reviewer_name_never_reaches_the_shard","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_log_redaction_reviewer_names.py:test_a_local_reviewer_name_never_reaches_the_shard"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5001,"diff_sha":"ab955e11b4137297ff0fed436b3dd3cf5b4f92d0c9e17876cdd782dcfc951c14","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-